{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "007E", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-stalks-abelian-presheaves}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6191f1cb9253d40e4e5ec9acc51e27e6fe9756cb1e85083688e81c883155d9a3", "source_text": "Stalks of abelian presheaves", "source_text_hash": "sha256:703bb3667dfc6ab26b65f3f6b00963c30d91a2c9f16565771390f997caaa986f", "unit_id": "tag:007E:title"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "007E", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:730e66c8892932a6045f7056a9f02e01133f725f8f7e345affae3f159de90b29", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe first deal with the case of abelian groups as\na model for the general case.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:24b68bd8dcbb021f9b5791ca362ca719a605e1b7516dfdea6ed6f7f70d7deba2", "unit_id": "tag:007E:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "007E", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}_x$", "MATH_0005": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0006": "$x\\in U$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}(U) \\to \\mathcal{F}_x$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n\\mathcal{F}_x\n=\n\\colim_{x\\in U} \\mathcal{F}(U)\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-stalk-abelian-presheaf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0df925dc128d847e9a8172e5d951e7278813e2c9c11dbd920d6e98e44e17bc4f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f1a7635282286e1c2dde0742797eafed55cfe9ee9d21f0f1cf6ef4edfe6d3bf6", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a topological space. Let <MATH_0002> be a presheaf\nof abelian groups on <MATH_0003>. There exists a unique structure of an\nabelian group on <MATH_0004> such that for every\n<MATH_0005> open, <MATH_0006> the map <MATH_0007>\nis a group homomorphism. Moreover,\n<MATH_0008>\nholds in the category of abelian groups.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:aa43b11342e91b940485b7182ca738191dfbc4189ab17029364b0b258603c95b", "unit_id": "tag:007F:statement"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "007E", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(U, s)$", "MATH_0002": "$(V, t)$", "MATH_0003": "$(U \\cap V, s|_{U\\cap V} +\nt|_{U \\cap V})$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c8f3d3cef5f7121e34389002f0bf43204ada8182edb96cf97d315c276138bb73", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0d8d8ff204f4030284632a2ba9131b634dc9aeee2d294d1ecfa5cafc656a2545", "source_text": "We define addition of a pair of elements\n<MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> as the pair <MATH_0003>. The rest is easy to check.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6697bb9b02a3b942bb11692fc95cbc2a35fb9420bd331a126c077bfc21f1a2aa", "unit_id": "tag:007F:proof"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "007E", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$A, B$", "MATH_0002": "$A \\oplus B$", "MATH_0003": "$A \\amalg B$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-definition-directed-set}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ab6036ee66c4403b189119ace51625f1220efc5ee174ffc9831ae86c051c0f3e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8b9d8e32eb6911d108f5f367f0bc5d757843359f2e5f1820daf47ab189662041", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWhat is crucial in the proof above is that the partially ordered set of open\nneighbourhoods is a directed set (Categories, Definition\n<REF_0001>). Namely, the coproduct\nof two abelian groups <MATH_0001> is the direct sum <MATH_0002>, whereas\nthe coproduct in the category of sets is the disjoint\nunion <MATH_0003>, showing that colimits in the category\nof abelian groups do not agree with colimits in the\ncategory of sets in general.\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a5dfbcd35204074ba5e33c946e29d60d4738d5cb3085b3477d5078853dc878a9", "unit_id": "tag:007E:prose-0002"}
